                <pb facs="0752" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">834.00 Revolutions/34: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Howard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-07T09:00:00-04:00">September 7, 1937—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. Have just arrived at Legation. Unconfirmed rumors allege that disturbances
                    due to the effort on the part of Minister of War to oust Minister of Interior.
                    President Paiva reported attempting some solution. Movement appears to be
                    assuming ex-combatant hue. Tension increasing.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Buenos Aires.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Howard</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
